      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 14 2019 19:02:04 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<div><span class=\"fontsize-2-5em\">&nbsp;</span></div>\n<div><span class=\"fontsize-2-5em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Improving safety</span><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">&nbsp;<br>\n Spreading truth about surgical smoke</span></span><br>\n</div>\n<div><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\">________________________________________</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 25 2021 18:27:33 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "default": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "2",
          "width": "8"
        }
      }
    },
    "text_copy_copy": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 14 2019 19:02:04 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<div>It’s such a startling statistic, many people can’t believe it’s true: One day in the operating room can have the same impact as smoking up to 27 unfiltered cigarettes<sup>1</sup>.&nbsp;<br>\n</div>\n<div><br>\nSurgical smoke happens when human tissue is contacted by lasers or electrosurgical devices, causing a toxic plume. In the United States, more than 59 million surgical procedures are performed every year, 85 percent of those procedures use laser or electrosurgical devices<sup>2</sup>. The risks it carries include chronic bronchitis, carcinoma, leukemia, cardiovascular dysfunction and more.&nbsp;</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 25 2021 18:14:53 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "default": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "2",
          "width": "5"
        }
      }
    },
    "text": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "bottomPadding": "5",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "leftPadding": "5",
      "topPadding": "5",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 25 2021 17:42:12 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span style=\"color: #ffffff;\">One day in the OR can have the same impact as smoking up to</span> </span><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">27 cigarettes</span><sup><span class=\"futura-bold\">1</span></sup></span></span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 26 2021 13:27:31 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "rightPadding": "5",
      "backgroundColor": "rgba(84,88,87,1)",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "default": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "width": "3"
        }
      }
    },
    "text_copy_copy_copy_": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 14 2019 19:02:04 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<div>The dangers of surgical smoke have been well-documented, yet regulations requiring facilities to evacuate surgical smoke are just emerging as states begin to take notice. As part of our mission to make healthcare better, Stryker is taking strong and active steps to make the OR a safe place for patients, surgeons and staff by:&nbsp;</div>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 25 2021 18:21:25 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "default": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "2",
          "width": "8"
        }
      }
    },
    "text_copy_copy_copy_626790476": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 14 2019 19:02:04 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><b><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Raising awareness&nbsp;</span></span></b><br>\n</div>\n<div>Surgical smoke is a threat every person should know about—not only in the healthcare setting but also across the general population. To raise awareness, we’re investing time, energy and resources into supporting this cause through educational campaigns, sharing real experiences and conducting MedEd courses which train close to 2,000 nurses per year. In addition, we are partnering with nursing organizations as they work to change policies to strengthen protection from surgical smoke in the workplace. &nbsp;</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Bringing innovation into the OR</span><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">&nbsp;</span></span><br>\nSurgical masks filter some particles, but not nearly enough. Up to 77% of the particles in surgical smoke are not adequately filtered out by standard surgical masks,<sup>3</sup> which is why we offer the Neptune SafeAir Smoke Evacuation Portfolio, designed to protect patients and staff from surgical smoke.&nbsp;</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 25 2021 18:20:56 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "default": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "2",
          "width": "5"
        }
      }
    },
