      "jcr:created": "Wed Sep 04 2019 20:35:31 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-8em\">1 – Hill D, O’Neill J, Powell R, Oliver D. Surgical Smoke - a health hazard in the operating theatre. A study to quantify exposure and a survey of the use of smoke extractor systems in UK plastic surgery units. Journ Plas Reconstr Aesthet Surg. 2012; 65(7): 911-6.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-8em\">2 – Ball K. No smoking in the OR. Outpatient Surgery. 2003. www.outpatientsurgery.net/_media/pop/print-article?id=4814. Accessed September 6, 2019.&nbsp;<br>\n &nbsp;<br>\n 3 – Katoch S, Venkataram M. Surgical Smoke in Dermatology: It’s Hazards and Management. J Cutan Aesthet Surg. 2019 Jan-Mar; 12 (1): 1-7.&nbsp;</span><b data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-8em\"><br>\n </span></b></p>\n",
